  "slug": "mitochondrial-resource-16ed",
  "summary": "Benchmarks, membrane protein and CNV resources, and pipeline validation frameworks now extend variant interpretation beyond missense scoring.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational infrastructure for interpreting human genetic variation, emphasizing standardized annotation, benchmarking and validation. Several preprints address specific variant classes. CNVSIM provides a copy-number reference atlas of 112 CNV-defined cancer subtypes with calibrated projection, and CNVision standardizes interpretation of intragenic CNVs by mapping breakpoints to coding sequences. memVar integrates roughly 10.9M ClinVar, COSMIC and gnomAD SNVs across 7,732 membrane proteins with topology and lipid-contact annotation. For missense variants, a leakage-controlled benchmark of variant effect predictors yields a gradient-boosting consensus model, and MetaDome 2027 aggregates evidence across homologous Pfam domains with GRCh38 support. An in silico framework tests clinical sequencing pipelines against planted truth variants. The new element is breadth: scope extends from missense scoring to structural copy-number variation, membrane-protein context and pipeline-level validation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-05"
}
